  "reason": "The largest performance jump in the history is from config_021 (singleprofile, no aggregation, concat: 0.535) to config_042 (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, concat: 0.599), a ~6-point gain. However, this comparison conflates two changes: (1) switching to multiprofile and (2) introducing transformer aggregation. Config_016 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) changes only the aggregation from transformer to avgpool while holding all other settings identical to config_042. This directly tests whether the transformer's sequential modeling of profiles is the critical driver or whether any aggregation of multiple profiles (even simple averaging) captures most of the gain. If avgpool approaches transformer performance, the multiprofile representation itself is the key factor (and a cheaper model suffices); if it falls well short, transformer aggregation is essential. This single-variable comparison is the most efficient way to reduce uncertainty about the aggregation design choice before committing further budget to the multiprofile+transformer family."
